    messageFontSize: 15
    noteFontSize: 14
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as API batch A
    participant B as API batch B
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over A,D: Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E
    Note over A,D: Both batches contain the same (source, event_id).<br/>Each batch sorts all event keys before writing.
    A->>D: BEGIN and INSERT usage_inbox identity
    D-->>A: New row, still uncommitted
    B->>D: BEGIN and INSERT the same identity
    Note over B,D: WAIT for the conflicting unique-index insertion
    alt A commits
        A->>D: COMMIT the complete batch
        D-->>B: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, no new row
        B->>D: Compare measurement fields<br/>FOR SHARE<br/>usage_inbox.source = S<br/>usage_inbox.event_id = E
        alt Same content
            B->>D: COMMIT, preserve the original received_at
            Note over B,D: Return 202, no duplicate usage_inbox row
        else Changed content
            B->>D: ROLLBACK the entire batch
            Note over B,D: Return 409 event_conflict<br/>Other new rows in B are also rolled back
        end
    else A rolls back
        A->>D: ROLLBACK and release the identity
        D-->>B: INSERT succeeds with B's usage_inbox row time
        B->>D: COMMIT before returning 202
    end
    Note over A,D: Sorted keys prevent opposite batch-key acquisition order.<br/>Disjoint event identities do not share this identity lock.
